# my_bot serial device names. Generated by scripts/setup_udev.sh on 2026-09-09T16:50:53+08:00.
# Regenerate after swapping hardware or moving a device to another USB port.
#
# WHICH IS WHICH, measured on the wire during that run rather than assumed:
#
#   1-2.1.4   (/dev/ttyUSB1) ESP32 -- answered `e` as: esp32
#   1-2.2     (/dev/ttyUSB0) lidar -- unprompted stream: lidar
#
# The ttyUSB numbers above are a snapshot and mean nothing later: they have
# already swapped once on this hardware. The port paths are the identity.
#
# Re-verify after any replug, in ten seconds:
#     scripts/motor_check.py --seconds 2.5   # or encoder_report.py --seconds 2
# Both refuse a port that streams unprompted, which is exactly the failure
# a crossed pair produces. Neither adapter has a unique serial (both are
# 10c4:ea60 reporting `0001`), so these rules match on physical USB port
# and are a promise about CABLING: move an adapter to another socket and
# its name silently follows the socket, not the device. Label the sockets.

# esp32 has no unique serial -- matched by USB port. Keep it in this port.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", KERNELS=="1-2.1.4", SYMLINK+="esp32", GROUP="dialout", MODE="0660"
# ydlidar has no unique serial -- matched by USB port. Keep it in this port.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", KERNELS=="1-2.2", SYMLINK+="ydlidar", GROUP="dialout", MODE="0660"
